JVM Mod Combiner
Copyright (c) 2026, hchunhei81-cyber

================================================================================
PROJECT NOTICE / 项目声明
================================================================================

This project (JVM Mod Combiner) is a Rust microkernel that hosts two
physically isolated Minecraft modding environments (Fabric and
Forge/NeoForge) inside separate JVMs, and synchronizes their state through
a Rust-owned data bus.

This software is experimental, research-oriented, and provided for
educational and development purposes only. It is NOT affiliated with,
endorsed by, or sponsored by Mojang Studios, Microsoft, FabricMC, or
NeoForged. "Minecraft" is a trademark of Mojang Synergies AB.

By using this software you acknowledge that:

  a) The software may launch, patch, or inject bytecode into third-party
     JVMs and game clients. You are solely responsible for complying with
     the terms of service and licenses of any third-party software
     (Minecraft, Fabric Loader, Forge, NeoForge, and any mods) that you
     run alongside it.

  b) Running two JVMs concurrently may cause high CPU/memory/GPU usage,
     system instability, or data loss. Use on production or important
     worlds at your own risk.

  c) The maintainers do not condone piracy or unauthorized distribution
     of game assets. This project does not bundle Minecraft assets.

  d) You must not use this software to circumvent copy protection,
     licensing, or access-control mechanisms of any third-party software.

This notice is informational only. The license terms below govern the
use, reproduction, and distribution of this source code.

